---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Modelling · Sundharesan Kumaresan">
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-6 pt-16 pb-16">
    <header class="border-t border-border pt-5">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
        <span class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-muted">An aspiration</span>
        <span class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-accent">Not yet</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="mt-5 font-serif font-semibold leading-[0.9]" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 5.5rem);">Modelling</h1>
    </header>

    <p data-reveal class="mt-8 max-w-[22ch] font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.05]" style="font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3.8vw, 2.25rem);">A portfolio page with nothing in it yet. On purpose.</p>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] md:items-center md:gap-16">
      <figure data-reveal class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[340px]">
        <div class="relative flex aspect-[4/5] w-full items-center justify-center border border-border">
          <span class="absolute left-3 top-3 h-2 w-2 bg-stellar"></span>
          <span class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-muted">No photo yet</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-text-muted">Nº 01 · unshot</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div data-reveal class="max-w-[56ch] space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>I've never modelled. No shoots, no catalogue, not one proper photo. What I do have is a stubborn hunch that I'd hold up in front of a camera, and every intention of finding out the day the chance shows up.</p>
        <p>So treat this as a placeholder for a version of me that doesn't exist on film yet. When there's something worth showing, it lands here. Until then the frame stays honest: empty.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
